>> title: Ox Tails, Instant Pot
>> category: Stews & Braises
>> tags: beef, braise, southern, gravy, instant pot, pressure cooker
>> counters: Instant Pot
>> dish: oxtails
>> kit: Instant Pot
>> aka: oxtails, ox tail, braised oxtails, smothered oxtails, oxtail and gravy, instant pot oxtails, pressure cooker oxtails
>> pairs-with: cheese-grits, collard-greens, butter-beans, hoppin-john
>> servings: 6
>> time: 1 hr 50 min
>> slack: forgiving — cut the natural release short and the meat tightens back onto the bone, and no extra pressure loosens it again
>> step.2: season, both sides
>> step.3: brown 15 min, in two batches
>> step.4: 45 min high pressure, natural release 20 min
>> step.5: skim, then slake the starch in

The lid takes the judgement away: forty-five minutes and a long natural release stand in for it.

Season @beef oxtails{4%lb}(1.8 kg; cut in sections) with @kosher salt{1%Tbs}, @black pepper{2%tsp}.

Brown @&(~1)seasoned oxtails{} in @vegetable oil{2%Tbs} on sauté in an #Instant Pot{} for ~brown{15%min}, in two batches, on the cut faces where the meat is.

Pressure cook @&(~1)browned oxtails{} with @yellow onions{2%large}(sliced), @garlic{6%cloves}(smashed), @carrots{2}(cut in chunks), @beef stock{2%cup}(475 mL), @dry red wine{1/2%cup}(120 mL), @bay leaves{2}, @dried thyme{1%tsp}, lid on and valve sealed: ~come to pressure{15%min}, then ~pressure cook{45%min} on high and ~natural release{20%min}.

Skim @&(~1)braised oxtails{}, then stir @cornstarch{1%Tbs}(8 g; slaked in 2 Tbs cold water) into the liquid on sauté for ~thicken{5%min}, lid off. Most of what is in the pot is gravy, so send it out over rice or over cheese grits.
